.claude/worktrees/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Derived from the evidence corpus; not committed, same as the raw evidence
# it derives from. `memoria normalize` regenerates them from the raw units it
# has a converter for; the rest of the retired Thoreau corpus's ingestion layer
# has no replacement yet (docs/open-problems.md 2.4). Ignored either way, so
# that records restored by hand or by the normalizer are not committed by
# accident.
sources/normalized/
sources/editorial/

# FTS5 search index; derived state, not durable (§42). Regenerate with
# `memoria rebuild` (see README).
.memoria/

# Machine-generated projection of the CHG- commits in git history; derived state,
# not durable (§42). Git remains canonical and `read(CHG-...)` renders from it
# directly, so these files are a browsing convenience and are never read back.
# Regenerate with `memoria rebuild` -- it needs no evidence root (ADR-0008).
changes/
